WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
Where do new beans come from?

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.600
Grow a bean from seed to seed and watch the cycle with your child.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.800
Over about three months, your child practices looking closely, measuring each week,

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.800
and checking a guess.

5
00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:18.853
Use untreated bush bean seeds.

6
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:21.813
Check for bean or legume allergies.

7
00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:25.173
Stay with your child when handling seeds.

8
00:00:26.373 --> 00:00:28.653
Keep loose seeds away from children under four.

9
00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:31.413
Call 911 if choking.

10
00:00:32.813 --> 00:00:34.993
Never taste the plant during the activity.

11
00:00:36.293 --> 00:00:39.393
Wash hands after handling soil, seeds, or plants.

12
00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:44.123
Gather potting mix and two or three pots with drainage holes.

13
00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:47.023
Soak one extra bean overnight.

14
00:00:48.323 --> 00:00:51.903
Help your child peel it and split it open to find the tiny leaves.

15
00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:54.883
Ask, “What do you think this will become?”

16
00:00:55.223 --> 00:00:56.543
Then toss the soaked seed.

17
00:00:57.583 --> 00:01:00.163
Dampen the potting mix before scooping it.

18
00:01:01.303 --> 00:01:03.943
Fill each pot to about two centimeters below the rim.

19
00:01:05.303 --> 00:01:08.123
Plant two or three seeds about three centimeters deep.

20
00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:11.663
Cover them and water until it drips out.

21
00:01:12.943 --> 00:01:18.743
Date the label. Use your sunniest window or plant outside after the last spring

22
00:01:18.743 --> 00:01:22.083
frost. Write down your child’s sprouting guess.

23
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:26.617
Visit together weekly for about ten to fifteen weeks.

24
00:01:27.937 --> 00:01:31.617
Measure the tallest plant with a ruler or with string and large blocks.

25
00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:34.397
Count leaves and draw the plant.

26
00:01:35.657 --> 00:01:37.617
Water when the soil surface feels dry.

27
00:01:38.877 --> 00:01:43.037
At about five centimeters, snip all but the strongest one or two yourself.

28
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.660
Before the flowers open, here is a question for you.

29
00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.140
Suppose your beans grow indoors on a sunny windowsill, with no bees at all.

30
00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.800
Will those flowers still make pods with new seeds, or stay empty?

31
00:02:03.833 --> 00:02:05.093
They can make pods.

32
00:02:06.753 --> 00:02:10.333
Bean flowers mostly pollinate themselves, often before opening.

33
00:02:11.693 --> 00:02:15.893
In warm weather, a hooked stem usually appears in five to fourteen days.

34
00:02:17.613 --> 00:02:20.813
Flowers usually open about four to seven weeks after planting.

35
00:02:22.253 --> 00:02:25.453
Ask your child, “What do you think will grow where the flowers are?”

36
00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:30.007
Tiny pods show up within a week or two of the first flowers.

37
00:02:31.547 --> 00:02:35.187
Green pods are ready to pick about seven to nine weeks after planting.

38
00:02:36.527 --> 00:02:40.927
For eating later, an adult boils picked green pods for at least thirty minutes.

39
00:02:42.147 --> 00:02:43.847
Leave at least three pods on the plant.

40
00:02:44.867 --> 00:02:48.987
Over the next three to six weeks, the pods dry and the seeds rattle.

41
00:02:50.447 --> 00:02:53.027
Ask, “Will the new seeds look like the one we planted?”

42
00:02:53.747 --> 00:02:57.807
Open a dry pod together and compare its seeds with one from the packet.

43
00:02:59.127 --> 00:03:01.927
After the seeds ripen, the plant yellows and dies.

44
00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.487
Divide a paper plate into five slices.

45
00:03:06.907 --> 00:03:11.627
Have your child draw a seed, a sprout, a leafy plant, flowers, and a pod with seeds.

46
00:03:13.027 --> 00:03:15.047
Draw an arrow from the pod back to the seed.

47
00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:20.227
Your child practices making a guess and checking it against what they saw.
